@startuml wal-segment-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
' WAL segment lifecycle — active → pending → rotated/truncated, and how a
' checkpoint advances checkpoint_lsn + truncates the WAL to the committed
' watermark while carrying commit_seq_floor across the rotation.
' Source of truth:
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/wal/pending_segment.rs  (PendingSegment carrier)
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/wal/header.rs           (checkpoint_lsn, commit_seq_floor)
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/wal.rs / wal_managed.rs (rotate / truncate)
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/overlay/durable_write.rs (committed watermark)
' Color key:  green #C8E6C9 = in-memory serving (appends land here)
'             blue  #BBDEFB = durable on-disk action (fsync / truncate / image)
'             amber #FFE0B2 = control / frontier (checkpoint, watermark, floor)
'             grey  #ECEFF1 = retired / infrastructure state
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title WAL segment lifecycle — append · rotate · checkpoint · truncate

[*] --> Active : create() / open()\n(fresh active segment,\ncommit_seq_floor seeded from header)

state Active #C8E6C9 : the writable segment\n• accepts record appends (LSN n, n+1, …)\n• each durable op: append + fsync, then root CAS\n• tracks next_lsn + the committed watermark
Active --> Active : append(WalRecord)\nLSN assigned, frame written

' --- background rotation path (async writer) -----------------------------
Active --> Pending : rotate\n(segment full / size threshold)
state Pending #FFE0B2 : PendingSegment\n• rotated away from the active writer\n• lsn_range = (first_lsn, last_lsn)\n• still awaits its background fsync
Pending --> Rotated : background fsync completes\n(records in this range are durable)
state Rotated #BBDEFB : durable, read-only segment\n(replayable on recovery)

note right of Pending #FFE0B2
  commit_seq_floor is CARRIED across the
  rotation: a fresh segment inherits the
  floor so post-rotation ops still out-rank
  pre-rotation survivors.
end note

' --- checkpoint path -----------------------------------------------------
Active --> Checkpointing : checkpoint()
state Checkpointing #BBDEFB {
  [*] --> WriteImage
  WriteImage : write the dense CX checkpoint image\n(durable point-in-time snapshot)
  WriteImage --> StampHeader
  StampHeader : header.checkpoint_lsn := committed watermark\n(largest L with every LSN ≤ L committed —\nthe ONLY safe checkpoint_lsn)\nheader.commit_seq_floor := max committed commit_seq
  StampHeader --> Truncate
  Truncate : truncate the WAL to checkpoint_lsn\n(records ≤ checkpoint_lsn are now subsumed\nby the image and reclaimed)
  Truncate --> [*]
}
Checkpointing --> Active : resume\n(new active tail begins just past checkpoint_lsn,\ncommit_seq_floor carried forward)

' --- shutdown ------------------------------------------------------------
Active --> Closed : drop() / close() (clean)
state Closed #ECEFF1 : segments flushed;\nheader's checkpoint_lsn + floor persisted
Closed --> [*]

legend right
| Color | Meaning |
|<#C8E6C9>| in-memory serving (appends) |
|<#FFE0B2>| control / frontier (checkpoint · watermark · floor) |
|<#BBDEFB>| durable on-disk action |
|<#ECEFF1>| retired / infrastructure |
endlegend
@enduml
